# Discriminating pair, HALF 1 of 2: a program the Cranelift JIT compiles and
# executes end to end. Its receipt must read `engine=cranelift-jit demoted=no`.
#
# Deliberately minimal: integer arithmetic and `print` only, no imports, so it
# does not depend on where the seed resolves the standard library from.
#
# CAUTION, and this is not hypothetical -- it happened while writing this file:
# the driver's pre-JIT gates test the ENTRY FILE'S SOURCE TEXT, not its
# semantics, so merely NAMING a trigger token in a COMMENT diverts the whole
# module to the interpreter. An earlier draft of this comment listed the tokens
# it was avoiding and thereby de-JIT'd itself, which the receipt caught
# immediately. That is the hazard in one line, and it is why this file names
# none of them. The tokens live in `demote_graphics_text.spl` and in
# `exec_core.rs`'s `interpreter_preference_reason`.
#
# Pairs with demote_graphics_text.spl. A receipt that says the same thing for
# both files is worthless, which is why the two are asserted together by
# scripts/check/check-engine-receipt-discriminates.shs.
fn main():
    var total = 0
    var i = 0
    while i < 10:
        total = total + i
        i = i + 1
    print "total={total}"
